codemap 8
path path-links
kind flow
author ai
group map
note How a step names another path that documents what its lines call, so shared code and work handed to another process are mapped once and read in place. The link is a field of the step, set by step-link and checked by Map::set_link: the target must exist and cannot be the step's own path. Renaming a path rewrites every link to it, a path that something links to cannot be removed, and check fails on a link to a missing path. path --expand and the GUI document show the linked path inline under the step.

